@startuml
title CycleFar — Make one workout Easier or Harder

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "PlannedWorkoutsController" as Controller
control "ManualEditor" as Editor
control "DirectionalAdjustment" as Selector
control "Generator, ExactDurationFitter\nand WorkoutCalculator" as Engine
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

Rider -> Controller: POST shuffle(action_kind: easier / harder)
Controller -> Database: load rider-owned workout with canonical steps
Controller -> Editor: apply!(action)
group owning plan lock / transaction
  Editor -> Database: lock plan; reload and validate planned structured regular workout
  Editor -> Database: read owner FTP, saved load adjustments\nand shared LoadContext progression ceiling
  Editor -> Editor: preview(action) in memory
  Editor -> Selector: call(canonical steps, subtype, duration, saved profile,\neffective level, ceiling, adjustments, FTP, TSS column scale)
  Selector -> Engine: calculate current metrics from canonical steps at current FTP
  Engine --> Selector: current TSS (not the stored estimate)

  alt subtype is in Training::Rules::LADDERS
    Selector -> Selector: Easier: lower levels nearest first\nHarder: higher levels nearest first\nthen current level; all within applicable ceiling
  else Endurance / Recovery: no ladder
    Selector -> Selector: one internal generator level-1 argument\nsearch aerobic profiles only
    note right of Selector
      ExactDurationFitter takes fit_aerobic;
      generated progression_level is nil.
      Endurance: sustained / alternating / undulating.
      Recovery: steady / gentle_ramp.
    end note
  end

  loop candidate levels and profiles until first qualifying replacement
    note over Selector, Engine
      At each level: saved profile first, then other profiles in declared order.
      Preserve subtype, exact duration, saved taper/target/filler/return limits.
    end note
    Selector -> Engine: generate candidate with explicit profile and saved adjustments
    Engine --> Selector: exact-duration canonical definition and fitted level
    alt Harder candidate fits below current effective interval level
      Selector -> Selector: skip candidate
    else candidate is eligible
      Selector -> Engine: calculate candidate metrics at the same FTP
      Engine --> Selector: candidate TSS
      Selector -> Selector: require calculated TSS AND displayed whole TSS\nto decrease for Easier / increase for Harder
      note right of Selector
        Display comparison: round to database
        decimal scale, then to a whole number.
        Reject wrong-direction and rounding-only changes.
      end note
    end
  end

  alt qualifying candidate found
    Selector --> Editor: selected definition and current/proposed metrics
    Editor -> Editor: retain workout purpose and automatic generation references
    group atomic workout replacement
      Editor -> Database: replace steps; save effective level, profile and metrics
    end
    Editor --> Controller: result (rest of plan unchanged)
  else all candidates exhausted
    Selector --> Editor: raise LimitReached (ArgumentError)
    Editor --> Controller: propagate limit; no persistence changes
  end
end

alt replacement saved
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to updated workout detail with success notice
else limit reached
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to unchanged workout detail with limit alert
end

note over Editor, Database
  No adaptation proposal, progression-bias update or completed-history mutation.
  The buttons apply immediately; there is no replacement-preview UI.
  ManualEditor#preview can select the same definition without writing records.
  Limit: No lower-load option is available at this duration.
  Try Shorter or Change workout. Harder uses higher-load and Longer.
end note
@enduml
